00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:03.909 align:start position:0%
2021 has been another incredible year  for the switch with nintendo delivering  plenty of quality titles for adults kids  and families alike my son and i have had  a great time with quite a few switch  games this year and today i'll share 10  of my favorites that would make  excellent gifts for your family and  don't worry i'll do a quick recap of all  10 games at the end of the video and  i'll also include links down in the  description below starting off our list  today we have super mario 3d world plus  bowser's fury while i think super mario  odyssey is still the best mario game on  the switch 3d world and bowser's fury  are more enjoyable for the whole family  up to four players can join in on the  fun as mario and his friends make their  way through an isometric 3d world which  has a slightly different camera from the  more traditional 3d mario titles 3d  world is a remake of the 2013 title for  the wii u which was praised for its  level design and gameplay that game  alone is certainly worth it but the  switch remake also includes bowser's  fury a brand new mario platforming  adventure featuring mario and bowser jr  this one can be enjoyed by two players  with one taking control of mario and the  other assisting is bowser jr the  gameplay is based on 3d world's  mechanics but also includes some  elements that are more similar to a game  like mario odyssey and then it also  includes some entirely new elements that  are fairly unique to the mario series  it's not really a long experience but my  son and i had a blast with it and it was  just a totally fresh take on the mario  formula even in 2021 the pokemon series  continues to be incredibly popular for  kids and while a brand new pokemon  experience is on the way next year in  2022 there are still two outstanding  pokemon titles that released this year  that kids would love to find under the  tree new pokemon snap released back at  the end of april as the long-awaited  sequel to an n64 classic the pokemon  snap series is quite different from the  mainline series and instead of having  players catch and battle pokemon they'll  instead be placed in the role of a  photographer who's helping pokemon  researchers there are various tactics  and strategies players will need to lure  pokemon out and get the best photograph  possible all the while taking the  pictures in the pokemon's native  habitats the game takes place in an  on-rails first-person perspective with  the player along for the ride and a  hovercraft there are more than 200  pokemon to photograph but one thing  parents and family should note is that  this is strictly a single player  experience if you're looking for a more  traditional pokemon experience 2021 will  see the release of pokemon brilliant  diamond and shining pearl this is a  remake of the 2006 nintendo ds game  featuring updated graphics and a few new  features as well you pretty much know  exactly what you're getting when it  comes to a mainline pokemon game diamond  and pearl are both quality entries to  the long-standing series and certainly  worth it for die hard fans even more so  if you've never played them before for  any parents who may be confused about  why there are two versions of the game  you don't need to purchase both for  years nintendo has a tradition of  releasing slightly different versions of  what's essentially the same game  starting all the way back with the  original pokemon red and blue it  basically comes down to a few pokemon  that are exclusive to specific versions  of the game including the legendary  pokemon featured on the cover if your  child is a big fan of the series it may  be a good idea to ask if they're wanting  a specific version first the game itself  though is the same experience across  both versions up next we have mario  party superstars now here's one where  you can get the whole family involved  superstars is the latest entry in the  long running series which is a  collection of mario themed mini games  where players earn points to move across  a virtual game board this one features  100 different mini games as well as 5  remade boards from the n64 trilogy of  games if you're looking for something a  little more outside the box than the  classic titles like mario party you  should check out mario kart live home  circuit this isn't your traditional  mario kart title though rather than all  of the action taking place on screen  home circuit is what they call a mixed  reality title which is where kids can  race physical carts throughout your home  on a track that players lay out  themselves each cart comes equipped with  a camera so players on the switch  actually see what their cart sees as  they race through the house and thanks  to a brand new update for mario kart  live multiplayer is now much easier  thanks to split screen in order to enjoy  multiplayer before this update you would  need two carts and also two nintendo  switches now you'll still need that  extra cart but you don't need a second  switch connect it to your tv and then  you'll be able to enjoy split screen  gameplay and both players can see their  carts racing throughout the house again  though you will still need that second  cart you can opt to purchase a mario  version just like the one you already  have or you can purchase the luigi  version instead nintendo also introduced  a new relay race mode which does allow  you to sort of have multiplayer with  just a single cart basically one player  controls the first lap and then they  switch control for the next lap to a  different player basically just taking  turns that being said this is definitely  one of those titles where kids will  enjoy taking turns because the person  not playing can keep track of the  physical cart that's moving throughout  the house now while home circuit may  stretch your budget a bit this next  title is one that can be found for  around 10 or 15 dollars considering it  released back in 2018. it's the  scribblenauts mega pack which includes  two previous scribblenauts games  unlimited and unmasked it's crazy i can  actually remember when the original  scribblemods launched on the nintendo ds  and it just absolutely blew my mind it  was so fun to try and come up with new  ways to solve the game's puzzles if you  aren't familiar with the scribblenauts  series players will control maxwell who  has a magical notebook that lets him  create seemingly any item he wants  players will use the notebook to  generate items into maxwell's world and  help him solve puzzles kids and honestly  adults too will love testing the limits  of the game to see just how far  maxwell's powers can go and what sort of  bizarre items they can create to help  solve the puzzle up next we have another  classic series that saw a new release in  2021 it's mario golf super rush i adored  the mario golf games as a kid so i was  thrilled to see nintendo bring this  popular series back for the switch with  super rush the visuals and mechanics are  as solid as ever and while this version  features new additions like speed golf  and a story adventure mode i still  believe mario golf is a game best  enjoyed with others and in this version  there are several multiplayer modes you  can enjoy with up to four players  locally of course the game supports  online multiplayer as well and while  there are certain parts of this game  that left fans a little bit disappointed  at the end of the day that rock solid  gameplay will keep you coming back for  more especially if you have friends or  family to play with now if you're  looking for something a bit more frantic  and fast paced the whole family can  enjoy concurrently check out overcooked  all you can eat which is a compilation  of both the original overcooked and  overcooked too i must admit i can't  promise this one won't result in some  shouting as you try and coordinate with  your family members to complete the  orders accurately and on time if you've  never played an overcooked game before  it doesn't take long for things to get  ridiculous  and hilarious the premise is simple  prepare food for customers in a given  amount of time the gameplay though not  so simple it'll throw plenty of  obstacles your way that make this much  easier said than done the level shift  change and add new elements as you  progress which only result in more  insane moments with overcooked you'll  probably want to check your competitive  ego at the door and just enjoy the  journey at this point what kid hasn't  heard of or played minecraft but what  about minecraft dungeons this game is a  spin-off to the classic minecraft and  instead of building and mining players  will hack and slash their way through a  minecraft world filled with traps  enemies and puzzles the game is  relatively short but the levels are  procedurally generated which can help  with things not getting stale too  quickly it's admittedly a simple game  but it's fun for kids and also when  families can enjoy together as it  supports up to four player co-op both  local and online this next title  appeared on last year's list but after a  massive update in 2021 animal crossing  new horizons earns another mention this  year as it remains one of the absolute  best switch games for families who  haven't played yet new horizons will  always hold a special place in my heart  given how much it helped my son and i  bond during the crazy year that was  2020. while our playing time has  certainly dwindled since then 2021 has  breathed new life into the game with a  huge dlc update this recent free update  brought back everyone's favorite barista  as brewster and his coffee shop finally  return there are also new items  customization options and numerous  quality of life improvements the update  also brought cooking and farming to the  game plus now players can grow  vegetables and use them to cook brand  new diy recipes now you may have also  heard there's a new paid dlc for animal  crossing called happy home paradise if  you want to add that update this dlc  gives players the chance to build  vacation homes and other buildings for  their villagers i'm also going to have a  video up for the best ps5 games for kids  which you can check out on the left side  of your screen now as always thank you  all so much for watching i'll talk to  you again soon  [Music]
 

